Section 166B: Procedure in case of refusal to give information

When a person is required under section 166A to give information regarding the commission of an offence, he shall give such information in writing in the form of a statement and shall sign such statement in the presence of the investigating officer;
Provided that if the person is not able to write, he shall make the statement orally before the investigating officer and such statement shall be written by the investigating officer in the presence of the person and one of the witnesses shall thereupon affix his signature in the presence of the investigating officer in lieu of the signature of the person;
Provided further that if the person is not able to make the statement in writing or orally, it shall be made available to him in such manner as the State Government may prescribe;
Provided also that if the statement is made in a language different from that of the Court, it shall be translated into the language of the Court.

