Section 35: Power of State Government to make rules

1[35. Power of State Government to make rules.--(1) The State Government may make rules regulating the conduct of drivers and passengers of motor vehicles with regard to the safety and comfort of the passengers and the public and enforcing such conduct.

(2) Without prejudice to the generality of the provisions of sub-section (1), rules may regulate--

(a) the conduct of drivers and passengers of motor vehicles, including the wearing of clothes by passengers of a sufficiently conspicuous colour to warn other road users of the presence of a motor vehicle and the carrying of luggage by passengers;

(b) the carrying of goods by passengers;

(c) the carrying of animals by passengers;

(d) the carrying of children by passengers;

(e) the carrying of motor cycles by passengers;

(f) the carrying of motor cycle drivers by passengers;

(g) the carrying of motor vehicles by passengers;

